[20:07:55] [TEST]   --- 1. Jia piecewise H_th method (Eq 8 + Eq 18) ---
[20:07:55] [PROCESS] Methodology: Four estimators are computed for comparison. (1) Jia piecewise H_th: H_{0,z_i} are fit by minimizing chi-squared with the cumulative piecewise Hubble parameter H_th(z) from Eq 8 and luminosity distance d_L from Eq 18, using MU_SH0ES with diagonal errors and no free M. Multiple restarts are used to avoid local minima from inter-bin correlations. (2) Free-M fit: M and H_{0,z_i} are fit simultaneously using m_b_corr with a Cepheid anchor (sigma_anchor = 0.15 mag). (3) Simple d_L: a single H_{0,z_i} is used for the entire integral, which is only correct for bin 1. (4) Simple inversion: per-SN H0 via LCDM inversion, binned by unweighted mean. Omega_m = 0.3 (fiducial). Six bins with edges [0.0, 0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.6, 1.0, 2.4].
